# The guard of board-keeps-drafts.drive, for edits a refused save left unsaved. tests/drive.rs
# installs the open-tasks example patched to open two notes whenever the tasks change. Another
# program leaves the canvas half written, so the card typed next can't be saved over it. A
# task written then makes the extension ask twice: the board stays in front and says that both
# were refused. Once the other program has finished the file, the card is merged into it and
# saved, and the next request opens its note. tests/drive.rs reads the canvas after.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for ☐ 16 open tasks
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter · ⏎ open · Esc back
type Drafts
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Drafts · 0 cards
write Drafts.canvas {"nodes":[
keys n
wait-for editing · type text · ⏎ new line · Esc done (saves)
type Kept through a refused save
keys esc
wait-for not saved: the file changed on disk and can't be read yet
screen
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n
wait-for ☐ 17 open tasks
wait-for open-tasks wanted to open Volcanoes/Vesuvius.md: not while the whiteboard's last edits aren't saved (2 requests refused)
expect whiteboard Drafts · 1 cards
screen
write Drafts.canvas {"nodes":[{"id":"theirs","type":"text","text":"Written elsewhere","x":0,"y":300,"width":260,"height":60}],"edges":[]}\n
wait-for whiteboard Drafts · 2 cards
screen
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n- [ ] Count the masks\n
wait-for ☐ 18 open tasks
wait-for Volcanoes/Vesuvius  reading
screen
keys esc
wait-for ? help  q quit
keys q
exits 0
